<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first prove
(<a href="#A2.E13" title="Equation B.13 ‣ Lemma B.1 (Uniform macroscopic coercivity). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.13</span></a>). It suffices to consider
<math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in C_{\rm c}^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in C_{\rm c}^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, the general case following by density and
closedness of the gradient.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that the conditional
density <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{-}</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{+}=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{+}=y</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{y}(u)\propto\exp\Bigl\{-V((y+u)/2)-\frac{\|y-u\|^{2}}{8\eta}\Bigr\}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.150em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{y}(u)\propto\exp\Bigl\{-V((y+u)/2)-\frac{\|y-u\|^{2}}{8\eta}\Bigr\}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">and define</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s_{y}(u)\coloneqq-\frac{1}{2}\,\nabla V((y+u)/2)-\frac{y-u}{4\eta}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≔</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.317em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{y}(u)\coloneqq-\frac{1}{2}\,\nabla V((y+u)/2)-\frac{y-u}{4\eta}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Differentiating the normalized conditional density gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f(y)=\mathrm{Cov}\bigl(f(Y_{-}),s_{y}(Y_{-})\bigm|Y_{+}=y\bigr)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f(y)=\mathrm{Cov}\bigl(f(Y_{-}),s_{y}(Y_{-})\bigm|Y_{+}=y\bigr)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
